# Built binaries. Anchored with a leading slash on purpose: a bare "slimproxy"
# pattern matches at any depth and matches directories, so it would silently
# ignore the entire cmd/slimproxy/ package -- the first commit would ship a
# repo with no main package and no warning from git.
/slimproxy
*.exe

# Generated on every start; contains inbound API keys. Per-port since two
# instances in one directory would otherwise overwrite each other's.
slimproxy.effective.yaml
slimproxy.*.effective.yaml

# Operator config; contains secrets. Commit slimproxy.example.yaml instead.
slimproxy.yaml

# OAuth credential material.
auths/

# Guard against stray credential copies landing in source directories. A real
# one was once found sitting next to credentials.go, where "git add ." would
# have staged it with the code; the package's own JSON fixtures live only in
# t.TempDir, so nothing legitimate matches this.
credentials/*.json

# Personal measurement artifacts from tunnel latency debugging.
deploy/argo-snapshots/

# Runtime state written by "slimproxy tunnel up -detach"
cloudflared.pid.json
cloudflared.log

# Logs. Not merely noise: logs/requests/ holds verbatim request and response
# bodies when request-log is on, and redaction there is header-name based only,
# so anything secret carried in a body is on disk in the clear. logs/ also
# receives stray-stdout.log in panel mode.
logs/
run.log

# Structured event stream. No bodies or headers, but it names credentials and
# hostnames, and it is covered by logs/ above -- listed here so the intent is
# explicit if logs/ is ever narrowed.
logs/events/

# Backups left by refactors, and the debris of interrupted builds.
_backup_*/
*.bak
*.bak-*
*~
